Build System
------------

- Class templates will all be in Rp namespace, but we may need to use
  different compilers for different source files.

- One option is to keep the *.cpp and *.cu files different directories, 
  so that they can create *.o files with the same name. This seems
  likely to be confusing to readers - we shouldn't need to maintain
  separate "build" directories with the src/ directory tree.

  Because the corresponding *.cpp and .cu files are already in different
  directories, it may be convenient to keep them there during other
  transformations, then move them at the end of the process.

- A better alternative:

    - Segregate files that instantiate specializations that use
      different compilers into files with different file name
      suffixes *.cpp, *.cu, *.hip etc.

    - Change the pattern rules for each suffix so as to create
      object files with different names, such as *_cpp.o, 
      *_cu.o, *_hip.o, etc.
     
  With this rule, we could keep everything in the rp directory.
  Consider renaming this rpd/, and then cpd/ for complex.

 
