Reducing need for specialization of classes templates defined in Rp
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  - Goal: Try to remove the need to re-implement virtual functions 
    in subclassses currently defined in Rpc and Rpg. Try to do this 
    wherever possible in the existing code, as prepatory step, before 
    attempting to change the entire type system. 

  - Comment: The main reason for such re-implemented subclasses is the 
    need to copy data between host and device in GPU code but not in CPU 
    code. We thus need to figure out to create some sort of function 
    template that behaves differently for CPU and GPU fields. 

  - Make RField etc. subclasses of a class DRArray that can have countable
    references, so that it is possible to create a zero-cost reference to
    a CPU field.

  - Create an alias for HostField in each Types class. Use DRArray for
    HostField in the Cpu variant.

  - Create a function template moveDeviceToHost and moveHostToDevice that 
    does an actual data copy for a GPU but simply creates a reference for 
    a CPU array.

  - As needed, some operations can be put inside if blocks that explicitly 
    check the enum that identifies which backend you are using. 

  - When we can't figure out how to get rid of the need for re-implemented
    virtual functions, change the name of the base class template by 
    adding a suffix "Base" to the base class name. This will ease the
    transition to a system in which base and derived classes will
    eventually live in the same namespace. 

